9|	 On each following day, repeat Step 8, monitor cells daily, and when confluence reaches ${\sim}80\%$ repeat Steps 1–7 (usually between 3 and 5 d after seeding). Passage the cells for the desired number of passages. After five passages, we recommend collecting some cells for FACS to measure pluripotency markers and for karyotyping. If the FACS and karyotyping results are satisfactory, the medium components are suitable for iPSC maintenance and reprogramming. This enzyme-free passaging protocol can be used during the derivation of iPSCs from other cell types. When you are ready to begin reprogramming, continue to the next section.
