## ANTICIPATED RESULTS
When human fibroblasts are reprogrammed in the E8-based feeder-free system, transformed cells are visible $5-6\mathrm{~d~}$ after transduction. It takes 20–30 d before true iPSC colonies mature enough for colony expansion (Fig. 2c). Overcrowded fibroblast cells often suppress the emergence of iPSC colonies, and thus EDTA dissociation could be used to differentially enrich iPSCs.
After mechanical isolation of iPSC colonies, EDTA dissociation enables effective expansion and cryopreservation in 1–2 weeks, markedly decreasing the time needed to preserve the cells. Owing to its simplicity, we are able to passage 24 individual lines from a 24-well plate in 15 min.
